[21.116977, "o", "NOTICES (supplier data)\r\n[\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"OPS-2288\",\r\n    \"severity\": \"info\",\r\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-11-10T08:00:00Z\",\r\n    \"title\": \"Maintenance window 2026-11-29\",\r\n    \"body\": \"The delta API is read-only on 2026-11-29 between 01:00 and 03:00 UTC. Cursors issued before the window stay valid; clients should retry with backoff.\"\r\n  },\r\n  {\r\n    \"id\": \"OPS-2291\",\r\n    \"severity\": \"action_required\",\r\n    \"published_at\": \"2026-11-18T06:30:00Z\",\r\n    \"title\": \"Schema v2.3: tombstones retire SKUs permanently - integrator action required for local price overrides\",\r\n    \"body\": \"From feed epoch 2026.47 (schema v2.3) a tombstone retires the SKU together with every downstream price attached to it, and retired SKU codes can be re-issued to a different product later in the same epoch (this delta contains re-issued codes). Local price overrides held for a tombstoned SKU are void: integrators must purge them when the tombstone is applied (e.g. DELETE FROM price_overrides WHERE sku = <tombstoned sku>), otherwise the"]
[21.117148, "o", " re-issued product inherits the old override and is sold at the retired item's promo/clearance price (double discount). Integrations that apply tombstones without purging overrides are out of contract for MAP pricing from 2026-11-25 (Integrator Agreement s4.2).\"\r\n  }\r\n]\r\n\r\n"]
